    paid_basis_invoice_ledger: 'Paid (invoices)',
    paid_basis_tip_invoice_ledger: "Every invoice recorded in the selected window that has since been settled, dated by the invoice's own recording date. No budget is consulted and the order's fate is not asked about: cash paid on an order withdrawn afterwards stays here.",
    paid_basis_note_invoice_ledger: 'This is the invoice ledger, not «Settled against plan» on Budgets: that counts only obligations the budget still carries, dated by the obligation and on the basis of the order itself. So the same invoice can be missing there, fall in another month, or carry a different amount. That is by design, not a defect.',
    paid_basis_budget_obligation: 'Settled against plan',
    paid_basis_tip_budget_obligation: "Settlement of obligations the budget still counts, dated by the obligation: request approval, or order issue/creation without a request. A department row takes the settlement whose date falls inside its own plan periods, so the plan beside it need not be the one that carried it; the org-wide row takes only what its own plans carried. Never added to actual spend. The amount is on the same basis as the columns to its left — each order's own VAT mode — so it reads against them. Analytics shows the invoice as billed, VAT included, so the figure there can differ.",
    paid_basis_note_budget_obligation: 'This is not «Paid (invoices)» on Analytics: that counts every settled invoice by the invoice date, regardless of plans and of what became of the order. So the same invoice can be there and missing here, or fall in another month. That is by design, not a defect.',
